          "text": "{\"edits\":[{\"start\":2,\"end\":3,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"Choose this earlier-arriving option if reaching Bangkok at 4:15 a.m. matters more than minimizing total elapsed time: it arrives 4 hours 35 minutes before the recommended option. It also has a 2-hour-30-minute LAX wait, 36 minutes shorter than the recommended option’s, but its Istanbul connection is 2 hours 20 minutes rather than 1 hour, and its reported elapsed time is 39 minutes longer.\"}]},{\"start\":6,\"end\":8,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"If you prefer to leave SFO in the morning rather than at 1:50 p.m., these 8:40 a.m. options arrive at the same time as the recommendation. Compared with it, they have a 37-minute shorter LAX wait, but a 7-hour Istanbul connection instead of 1 hour and a reported elapsed time 5 hours 10 minutes longer. The two results otherwise share the displayed schedule and award details; their positioning flights differ: Alaska on one, United on the other.\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J115@2027-01-08T08:40-08:00/SFO>BKK/B>2027-01-10T08:50\",\"n\":\"Morning departure, United positioning flight\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at 8:40 a.m. on January 8 and arrives in Bangkok at 8:50 a.m. on January 10. The award portion is reported in business cabin and costs 275,000 Turkish-program points; individual leg cabins are not specified. The separately booked SFO–LAX positioning flight is on United, followed by a 2-hour-29-minute wait at LAX; the award itinerary connects at Istanbul for 7 hours. Seat-count evidence and award taxes are unavailable, and the quote scope is unknown. Separate-ticket protection, traveler applicability, and positioning permission are unverified.\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J105@2027-01-08T08:40-08:00/SFO>BKK/B>2027-01-10T08:50\",\"n\":\"Morning departure, Alaska positioning flight\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at 8:40 a.m. on January 8 and arrives in Bangkok at 8:50 a.m. on January 10. As with the other 8:40 a.m. option, the award portion is reported in business cabin and costs 275,000 Turkish-program points, with individual leg cabins unspecified. Its separately booked SFO–LAX positioning flight is on Alaska, followed by a 2-hour-29-minute LAX wait; the award itinerary connects at Istanbul for 7 hours. The displayed advantage over the United-positioning result is the carrier choice for the positioning flight, not a timing difference. Seat-count evidence and award taxes are unavailable, and quote scope is unknown; separate-ticket protection, traveler applicability, and positioning permission are unverified.\"}]}]}",
